profile: minimodel.workspace.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-08-28T00:00:00Z
site: MiniModel.org
status: prelaunch-catalog-authority
current_authority:
  - MiniModel.org publishes bounded discovery metadata and does not proxy model bytes.
  - Exact qualified SLM2 compositions move directly between consenting peers; otherwise an installed local companion performs explicit pinned local conversion.
  - Catalog identity, qualification, peer availability, transfer, browser activation, and publication are separate claims.
  - Read .uai/totem.uai, .uai/taboo.uai, and docs/catalog-boundary.md before changing behavior or claims.

memory_endpoints_two_lane_authority:
  direct_agent_coordination: Agents working on all ecosystem sites use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination.
  tinyrustlm_connect_user_plugin: Separately, the TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin lets a user sign in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly select it as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  isolation: Keep lane identity, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts separate. MemoryEndpoints.com is not a model-byte transport, peer relay, catalog authority, or inference service.
  proof_boundary: Authorization, configuration, fixtures, mocks, or reachability do not prove live memory, peer availability, synchronization, restore, deletion, cleanup, or continuity.

prelaunch_redundancy:
  policy: Important memory may also be kept in current .uai, wiki, public-safe source notes, and approved private stores for resilience.
  invariant: Every maintained copy stays current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  conflict_rule: Surface and reconcile conflicts; do not silently choose one contradictory copy.
